From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] AUTO_MEMORIES: a macro's blackbox costs its generated view's area
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With SYNTH_MINIMUM_KEEP_SIZE, synthesis picks the modules to keep with
keep_hierarchy -min_cost, which needs a cost for every instanced
blackbox. convert_liberty_areas gives Liberty cells one, but an
AUTO_MEMORIES macro is a blackbox made from the RTL's own module and has
none: any AUTO_MEMORIES design with a keep threshold stopped with
"Missing cost information on instanced blackbox".

blackboxes.txt now carries `<module> <area>` per line, the area the
generated .lib states, and synthesis gives each AUTO_MEMORIES blackbox
that area's gate equivalent. A listed module that is in the design but
not a blackbox is an error: its name did not match its definition.

This is The-OpenROAD-Project/OpenROAD-flow-scripts#4650 at its head
(a3305f118b), applied on the patches carried before it. Beyond the
upstream pull request, so the carried tree stays consistent, FakeRAM's
spsram_mask_test (patch 0073) reads the new line format.

Not upstreamed yet; retires at a bump onto an ORFS that carries #4650.
---
